      <p>My experience with random chat platforms taught me that the platform itself is only one part of online safety. The way a user handles personal information, suspicious requests, uncomfortable conversations, and privacy settings matters just as much.</p>

      <p>One of the biggest lessons is to avoid assuming that someone is trustworthy simply because a conversation feels friendly. A good conversation can still be enjoyable without sharing personal details or moving immediately to another platform.</p>

      <p>That mindset changed how I approach random conversations: stay curious, but keep reasonable boundaries.</p>

